# The End, voice leading of the B# diminished seventh into A (figure 191.2)
# Pollack's four lines, top to bottom: F# and D# both to E, B# up to C#, A held (the bass).
# The chord names are added (from fig. 191.1). Octaves are a plain close voicing over A3.
key A

system
voice    | F#4 | E4 |
voice    | D#4 | E4 |
voice    | B#3 | C#4 |
bass     | A3 | - |
chords   | B#dim7/A | A |
